{"id":"addback-by-budget","title":"What the Board adds to the budget each June","question":"How much money does the Board of Supervisors move into its own spending list each year, and can a reader tell who gets it?","finding":"Across 13 budgets the Board’s lists add $454.2 million for the first year alone, peaking at $99.0 million in June 2021 and falling to $19.3 million in June 2026; of 2,036 lines, 16 name an organisation the City pays.","how":"One document per budget: the final add-back list or spending plan attached to the budget ordinance. First-year amounts are added up; where a list prints one citywide line for the district items, that line is used and the district breakdown is not added again.","limits":"An add-back is a budget act, and the City Attorney’s memos say a line may give the amount, department and purpose but not a named grantee. Five lists are scans read by machine; 2016 and 2017 recover under 90% of the printed total, so those years are understated. Second-year amounts are usually decided again the next June. The 2019 list also carried a separate $298 million plan for one-off property-tax money, not counted here.","tier":"REDFLAG","columns":[{"k":"budget","t":"Budget adopted","type":"text"},{"k":"lines","t":"Lines","type":"int"},{"k":"firstYear","t":"Added, first year","type":"usd"},{"k":"secondYear","t":"Added, second year","type":"usd"},{"k":"districtShare","t":"Share for district lists","type":"pct"},{"k":"oneTimeShare","t":"Marked one-time (where the list has that column)","type":"pct"},{"k":"named","t":"Lines naming an organisation","type":"int"},{"k":"reading","t":"How it was read","type":"text"},{"k":"doc","t":"Source","type":"link"}],"rows":[{"budget":"June 2014","year":"2014","lines":171,"firstYear":23139109,"secondYear":18394629,"district":11153631,"districtShare":0.482,"oneTimeShare":null,"named":0,"reading":"text of the document","doc":{"t":"spending list","u":"https://sanfrancisco.legistar1.com/sanfrancisco/attachments/74754.pdf"}}